WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900
Ten leaves grew on the same oak.

2
00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.400
Why do they share rounded lobes but differ in size and shape?

3
00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.240
Their story begins with variation.

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.480
Look closely as each leaf settles beside the ruler.

5
00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:20.047
A trait is a feature, like leaf shape or height.

6
00:00:21.327 --> 00:00:25.647
A population is a group of the same kind of living thing in one area.

7
00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:29.687
Variation means differences among its members.

8
00:00:31.307 --> 00:00:34.227
Shared traits and differences can exist at the same time.

9
00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.890
Two routes shape many traits.

10
00:00:38.090 --> 00:00:40.870
Blue inherited information comes from parents.

11
00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:46.610
Green environmental conditions include food, health, sunlight, and water.

12
00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.410
The routes often act together.

13
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.210
For many traits, both matter.

14
00:00:53.283 --> 00:00:54.903
Height shows both routes.

15
00:00:56.203 --> 00:00:57.823
Many genes contribute to height.

16
00:00:59.403 --> 00:01:01.403
Food and health during childhood matter too.

17
00:01:03.023 --> 00:01:07.083
Similar inherited information does not guarantee exactly the same height.

18
00:01:08.403 --> 00:01:10.963
A height bar is not a prediction for one person.

19
00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:16.627
Sexual reproduction reshuffles alleles already present in the parents.

20
00:01:17.927 --> 00:01:20.147
Picture blue cards dealt into new hands.

21
00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.607
The combinations are new, but the cards already existed.

22
00:01:26.047 --> 00:01:29.007
Siblings can receive different mixes from the same parents.

23
00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:32.230
Mutation adds a different route.

24
00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:37.330
A mutation changes the DNA sequence, the order of its bases.

25
00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:40.290
That change can make a new allele.

26
00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.190
It may change a protein, its amount, or neither.

27
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.840
Copying mistakes, radiation, or some chemicals can cause mutations.

28
00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.060
The change does not appear because a living thing needs its effect.

29
00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.300
Need sends no instructions backward.

30
00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.640
More exposure can raise chance without choosing the result.

31
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:10.393
Now predict. Two children inherit very similar height alleles, but their food and

32
00:02:10.393 --> 00:02:14.133
health differ. Must they reach exactly the same height?

33
00:02:15.453 --> 00:02:19.613
Hold your answer. Watch both coloured routes before you decide.

34
00:02:25.617 --> 00:02:31.897
No. Genes and environment act together, so different conditions can lead to

35
00:02:31.897 --> 00:02:32.897
different heights.

36
00:02:33.777 --> 00:02:37.157
This does not prove which route caused any one person's height.

37
00:02:38.417 --> 00:02:41.577
The picture shows a possibility, not that child's history.

38
00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:47.350
In animals that reproduce with eggs and sperm, location also matters.

39
00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.410
A mutation in a body cell stays in that body.

40
00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.610
A mutation in an egg or sperm can reach offspring.

41
00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.930
The path, not usefulness, decides whether inheritance is possible.

42
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.460
Follow the full picture.

43
00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.020
Shared traits can vary.

44
00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:10.720
Inherited information and environment shape that variation.

45
00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.960
Chance mutation can add a new genetic difference.

46
00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.500
This rule does not make every visible difference inherited.

47
00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:23.093
A new difference still has no fixed label.

48
00:03:24.513 --> 00:03:27.773
Next, ask whether its effect changes when the surroundings change.

49
00:03:28.913 --> 00:03:30.653
That is the second film's puzzle.
